Chad

You are correct that we would like to have stratum-specific multipliers.  As you note, this is a limitation of our current software.

The work-around would be to perform the point and variance estimation for multipliers by hand.  You know that the formulas for the point estimates are straightforward; the variance estimation is only slightly more difficult.  Have a look at Eqn. 6.6 of Buckland et al. (2001).

