Following up on Eric's reply, there is an easier work-around, but it doesn't allow you to incorporate uncertainty in the g(0) estimates.  Effort in line transect sampling is usually the line length.  Suppose you had a line of 4km, and estimated g(0) to be 0.75.  You can multiply the line length by g(0), and analyse the data as if effort was 4*0.75 = 3km.  The multiplier could then be different for each line.

Steve Buckland

