MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hi Dan,

This sounds reasonable to me since the ransom starting point should ensure that you are not influencing your transect lengths or placements by an expectation of target presence or abundance. If you lose a lot of effort ferrying, and the resultant reduced survey coverage lowers your estimate precision, I do not see the benefit of NOT using your proposed approach.

Regards,  Jack

