Hi,

I've been following Miller et al. 2013 "Spatialmodels for distance sampling data: recent developments and future directions" (Meth Eco & Evo) to apply a DSM to my data on São Tomé dwarf olive ibis.

I've done my best to make sure my data fits the recquirements of "dsm", but when I try to run the model I get an error

"> mod1 <- dsm(N ~ s(x, y, k=4), hnmodel$ddf, sega, obsa)
Error in aggregate.data.frame(as.data.frame(x), ...) :
  no rows to aggregate"

"sega" and "obsa" correspond to Miller's "segdata" and "obsdata", respectively, and have the following structure:
